agree with your description of Abbatoir. The movie fell flat, but the ideas behind it were pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T16:55:15-07:00","id":1074404,"title":"","content":"I actually remember Flatliners when it first came out...makes me feel old, but yeah i love the tagline to that movie &quot;It's a good day to die&quot;. I will have to check out We Go On. I thought Odd Thomas was interesting as well specially the way he could see the other creatures and such that 'normal' people could not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":12143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","user":"EldritchMinister","date":". 04-06-2017, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T16:59:01-07:00","id":1074406,"title":"","content":"There's Truly Madly Deeply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T08:56:34-07:00","id":1075492,"title":"","content":"How has nobody mentioned The Crow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:31:48-07:00","id":1075644,"title":"","content":"For me, the best &quot;Geist&quot; movie has always been The Frighteners.<br /> <br /> Protagonist that gains the ability to interact with ghosts after a close-death experience? Check.<br /> <br /> Ghosts that cling to the mortal realm because of their connection to the living world but can be forced to leave by sheer force? Check<br /> <br /> Using your powers over ghosts for personal gain because you might as well do it? Check<br /> <br /> The ability to spot Death Marks? Check<br /> <br /> I could keep going, but really, check that movie. It's also a good one, and the Dark Eras chapter about Geist suggests it as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=